+  <h2 class="label bring-title">What I bring</h2>
+  <ul class="bring">
+    <li><b>Pipelines that join messy data from several sources.</b> I matched two satellites with different resolutions and overpass times across 100+ scenes. <a href="#stage-1">Stage 1</a></li>
+    <li><b>Fast, validated stand-ins for slow models.</b> I replaced a physics solver with ML emulators checked against held-out data, fast enough for millions of pixels. <a href="#stage-2">Stage 2</a></li>
+    <li><b>Honest evaluation.</b> I document where a method fails and what is still above target, like the regression that could not separate aerosol from albedo and the RMSE that misses the target. <a href="#stage-1">Stage 1</a>, <a href="#stage-3">Stage 3</a></li>
+    <li><b>Explaining technical work plainly.</b> I've presented research as a poster and slides, and each project here starts with a plain-language summary. <a href="poster.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Poster</a></li>
